{"links":{"self":"/authors/OL3110634A/works.json","author":"/authors/OL3110634A"},"size":13,"entries":[{"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":""From the critically acclaimed author of Sea of Rust and Queen of the Dark Things comes a hair-raising collection of short fiction that illuminates the strange, humorous, fantastical, and downright diabolical that tantalize and terrorize us: demons, monsters, zombie dinosaurs, and Death itself. In the novella "The Soul Thief's Son" C. Robert Cargill returns to the terrain of the Queen of the Dark Things to continue the story of Colby Stevens. A Triceratops and an Ankylosaurus join forces to survive a zombie apocalypse that may spell extinction for their kind in "Hell Creek". In a grand old building atop a crack in the world, an Iraq War veteran must serve a one-year term as a punisher of the damned condemned to consume the sins of others in the hope that one day he may find peace in "In a Clean, White Room" (co-authored with Scott Derrickson). In "The Town That Wasn't Anymore," the village of Pine Hill Bluff loses its inhabitants one at a time as the angry dead return when night falls to steal the souls of the living. And in the title story, "We Are Where the Nightmares Go," a little girl crawls through a glowing door beneath her bed and finds herself trapped in a nightmarish wonderland--a crucible of the fragments of children's bad dreams. These tales and four more are assembled here as testament to Cargill's mastery of the phantasmagoric, making We Are Where the Nightmares Go and Other Stories a collection of unnerving horror and fantasy will keep you up all night and haunt your waking dreams"--

"From the critically acclaimed author of Sea of Rust comes a collection of short stories and novellas spanning the strange, humorous, fantastical, and downright diabolical"--"},"key":"/works/OL19748029W","title":"We Are Where The Nightmares Go","authors":[{"type":{"key":"/type/author_role"},"author":{"key":"/authors/OL3110634A"}}],"type":{"key":"/type/work"},"covers":[9303067],"subjects":["Fiction, horror","Fiction, short stories (single author)"],"genres":["/tags/OL171T"],"latest_revision":7,"revision":7,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2019-05-24T08:35:21.510183"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2026-09-07T22:20:04.807100"}},{"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":""Six months have passed since the wizard Colby lost his best friend to an army of fairies from the Limestone Kingdom, a realm of mystery and darkness beyond our own. But in vanquishing these creatures and banning them from Austin, Colby sacrificed the anonymity that protected him. Now, word of his deeds has spread, and powerful enemies from the past--including one Colby considered a friend--have resurfaced to exact their revenge. As darkness gathers around the city, Colby sifts through his memories desperate to find answers that might save him. With time running out, and few of his old allies and enemies willing to help, he is forced to turn for aid to forces even darker than those he once battled"--"},"covers":[7983637],"key":"/works/OL17708650W","authors":[{"type":{"key":"/type/author_role"},"author":{"key":"/authors/OL3110634A"}}],"title":"Queen of the dark things","subjects":["Imaginary places","Goblins","Magic","Best friends","Fairies","Wizards","Fiction","Fiction, fantasy, general","Imaginary places, fiction"],"type":{"key":"/type/work"},"genres":["/tags/OL169T"],"latest_revision":5,"revision":5,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2017-05-06T05:29:26.199908"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2026-09-04T18:43:24.390918"}},{"type":{"key":"/type/work"},"title":"Sea of Rust","authors":[{"type":{"key":"/type/author_role"},"author":{"key":"/authors/OL3110634A"}}],"covers":[11301891],"key":"/works/OL24626070W","latest_revision":2,"revision":2,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2021-06-25T03:51:29.058297"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2022-04-07T22:39:18.657698"}},{"subjects":["Fiction, science fiction, general","Fiction, dystopian","Fiction, fantasy, general"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":""A scavenger robot wanders in the wasteland created by a war that has destroyed humanity in this evocative post-apocalyptic "robot western" from the critically acclaimed author, screenwriter, and noted film critic. It's been thirty years since the apocalypse and fifteen years since the murder of the last human being at the hands of robots. Humankind is extinct. Every man, woman, and child has been liquidated by a global uprising devised by the very machines humans designed and built to serve them. Most of the world is controlled by an OWI--One World Intelligence--the shared consciousness of millions of robots, uploaded into one huge mainframe brain. But not all robots are willing to cede their individuality--their personality--for the sake of a greater, stronger, higher power. These intrepid resisters are outcasts; solo machines wandering among various underground outposts who have formed into an unruly civilization of rogue AIs in the wasteland that was once our world. One of these resisters is Brittle, a scavenger robot trying to keep a deteriorating mind and body functional in a world that has lost all meaning. Although unable to experience emotions like a human, Brittle is haunted by the terrible crimes the robot population perpetrated on humanity. As Brittle roams the Sea of Rust, a large swath of territory that was once the Midwest, the loner robot slowly comes to terms with horrifyingly raw and vivid memories--and nearly unbearable guilt. Sea of Rust is both a harsh story of survival and an optimistic adventure. A vividly imagined portrayal of ultimate destruction and desperate tenacity, it boldly imagines a future in which no hope remains, yet where a humanlike AI strives to find purpose among the ruins"--

"In this post-apocalyptic "robot western," critically acclaimed author, screenwriter, and noted film critic C. Robert Cargill brilliantly chronicles the tale of a scavenger robot wandering in the wasteland left after the war that destroyed humanity"--"},"key":"/works/OL19720087W","title":"Sea of rust","authors":[{"type":{"key":"/type/author_role"},"author":{"key":"/authors/OL3110634A"}}],"type":{"key":"/type/work"},"genres":["/tags/OL179T","/tags/OL169T"],"latest_revision":5,"revision":5,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2019-05-23T23:48:11.257816"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2026-08-30T14:34:02.349703"}},{"type":{"key":"/type/work"},"title":"Day Zero","authors":[{"author":{"key":"/authors/OL3110634A"},"type":{"key":"/type/author_role"}},{"author":{"key":"/authors/OL7881269A"},"type":{"key":"/type/author_role"}}],"covers":[11965251],"key":"/works/OL25075725W","latest_revision":3,"revision":3,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2021-09-15T13:43:48.039129"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2022-04-07T22:39:18.657698"}},{"type":{"key":"/type/work"},"title":"We Are Where the Nightmares Go and Other Stories","subjects":["Fiction, short stories (single author)","Fiction, horror"],"authors":[{"type":{"key":"/type/author_role"},"author":{"key":"/authors/OL3110634A"}}],"key":"/works/OL27120311W","genres":["/tags/OL171T"],"latest_revision":2,"revision":2,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2022-01-28T06:59:24.692474"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2026-08-26T11:06:34.705696"}},{"type":{"key":"/type/work"},"title":"Day Zero","authors":[{"type":{"key":"/type/author_role"},"author":{"key":"/authors/OL3110634A"}}],"covers":[10606346],"key":"/works/OL24181763W","subjects":["American literature"],"latest_revision":2,"revision":2,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2021-02-04T19:23:36.804136"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2021-12-27T10:57:00.664365"}},{"title":"Sea of Rust","subjects":["Fiction, science fiction, general","Robots","Fiction","Artificial intelligence"],"key":"/works/OL21622637W","authors":[{"type":{"key":"/type/author_role"},"author":{"key":"/authors/OL3110634A"}}],"type":{"key":"/type/work"},"covers":[10871926],"genres":["/tags/OL179T"],"latest_revision":4,"revision":4,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2020-08-25T05:35:23.289397"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2026-08-29T08:04:13.300915"}},{"title":"Queen of the Dark Things","subjects":["Fiction, fantasy, general","Imaginary places, fiction"],"key":"/works/OL21470942W","authors":[{"type":{"key":"/type/author_role"},"author":{"key":"/authors/OL3110634A"}}],"type":{"key":"/type/work"},"genres":["/tags/OL169T"],"latest_revision":2,"revision":2,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2020-08-21T23:36:32.848836"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2026-09-01T08:03:04.812076"}},{"title":"Robo sapiens: Roman","created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2019-09-20T07:36:19.760379"},"covers":[8785965],"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2019-09-20T07:36:19.760379"},"latest_revision":1,"key":"/works/OL20135256W","authors":[{"type":{"key":"/type/author_role"},"author":{"key":"/authors/OL3110634A"}}],"type":{"key":"/type/work"},"revision":1},{"title":"Dreams and shadows","subjects":["Magic","Fiction","Imaginary places","Fiction, fantasy, general","Fiction, horror"],"key":"/works/OL19960934W","authors":[{"type":{"key":"/type/author_role"},"author":{"key":"/authors/OL3110634A"}}],"type":{"key":"/type/work"},"covers":[10493574],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":""There is another world than our own-- one no closer than a kiss and one no further than our nightmares-- where all the stuff of which dreams are made is real and magic is just a step away. But once you see that world, you will never be the same. Dreams and Shadows takes us beyond this veil. Once bold explorers and youthful denizens of this magical realm, Ewan is now an Austin musician who just met his dream girl, and Colby, meanwhile, cannot escape the consequences of an innocent wish. But while Ewan and Colby left the Limestone Kingdom as children, it has never forgotten them. And in a world where angels relax on rooftops, whiskey-swilling genies argue metaphysics with foul-mouthed wizards, and monsters in the shadows feed on fear, you can never outrun your fate" -- from HarperCollins web site."},"genres":["/tags/OL169T","/tags/OL171T"],"latest_revision":6,"revision":6,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2019-07-17T23:03:21.431776"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2026-09-01T06:32:20.913970"}},{"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2019-06-26T14:39:15.855487"},"subjects":["Fantasy games"],"latest_revision":1,"key":"/works/OL19820614W","title":"Tome of artifacts","authors":[{"type":{"key":"/type/author_role"},"author":{"key":"/authors/OL2660525A"}},{"type":{"key":"/type/author_role"},"author":{"key":"/authors/OL2876057A"}},{"type":{"key":"/type/author_role"},"author":{"key":"/authors/OL3110634A"}},{"type":{"key":"/type/author_role"},"author":{"key":"/authors/OL3082832A"}},{"type":{"key":"/type/author_role"},"author":{"key":"/authors/OL3110635A"}}],"type":{"key":"/type/work"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2019-06-26T14:39:15.855487"},"covers":[1963340],"revision":1},{"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2019-03-27T10:57:39.697328"},"subjects":["Magic","Fiction"],"latest_revision":2,"key":"/works/OL19357968W","title":"Dreams and Shadows","authors":[{"type":{"key":"/type/author_role"},"author":{"key":"/authors/OL3110634A"}}],"type":{"key":"/type/work"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2020-06-11T07:33:17.455413"},"covers":[8472459],"revision":2}]}
